description:
@cucumber/gherkin 42.0.1 is ESM-only. scripts/spec-audit.ts is compiled to CommonJS by ts-node, so requiring it needs Node's require(esm), which exists only from 20.19 and 22.12. On Node 18 the audit crashes at startup with ERR_REQUIRE_ESM.

This is invisible today because the EARS Spec Audit CI job pins Node 20, but package.json declares engines node >=18.0.0 and the unit test matrix covers Node 18, so a contributor on Node 18 cannot run npm run spec:audit at all. The audit's own fixture suite detects the condition and skips with a warning rather than asserting against a startup error.

Decide one of: raise the documented dev-tooling Node floor to 20.19; load gherkin via a dynamic import that survives CommonJS downleveling; or pin gherkin to the last CJS major. Note the same constraint applies to the Phase 2 plan of porting the Hermes step checks into this script.
